  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.form1040-line16",
  "notes": "Form 1040 Line 16 v4 (ADR-0052 Decision 4/7): identifier substitution selected_line7a -> selected preferential base, per the ledger in ADR-0052 Decision 6. The common set (taxable income, filing status, rounding, qualified dividends, selected preferential base) is required unconditionally; a blocked or inapplicable selected preferential base is DEPENDENCY_ABSENT here exactly as v3 already propagated a blocked/guard_inapplicable line 7a. The branch-specific ADR-0050 Decision 7 declaration/conclusion pins (the four-row table) apply only when the eligible-family proceeds companion is closed-empty (the direct-producer branch, tested the same way rule.selected-preferential-base tests it): closed-nonempty (Schedule-D producer) reads neither the checked conclusion nor capital-gain-distributions at all - the common set alone, per ADR-0052 Decision 4. QDCG-vs-ordinary selection itself (Q>0 or L>0) is unchanged from v3 and is not branch-conditioned. v1/v2/v3 remain historical.",
